TUTORIALS.append({'title': 'CP-1. Setup: folders, INSTALLED_APPS, urls', 'category': 'programming', 'order': 1, 'summary': 'Do this first: the app layout and settings.', 'content': '<p>Step 1 of 9. Create the app folder with this layout. <code>__init__.py</code> is empty. Add <code>"cprofile"</code> to <code>INSTALLED_APPS</code> and include its urls. There are no models, so no migrations.</p>\n<p>Needs <code>oracledb</code> and <code>openpyxl</code> (both already in the project). In <code>queries.py</code> change the line <code>from main.oracle import get_oracle_connection</code> to where your function lives. Add a sidebar link to <code>{% url \'client-portfolio\' %}</code> in base.html.</p>\n<h3>Layout</h3>\n<pre><code class="language-plaintext">cprofile/\n    __init__.py\n    apps.py\n    urls.py\n    queries.py\n    accounts.py\n    logic.py\n    excel.py\n    views.py\n    templates/cprofile/page.html\n</code></pre>\n<h3>urls.py of the project</h3>\n<pre><code class="language-python">path("cprofile/", include("cprofile.urls")),\n</code></pre>\n'})

